{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Choir Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a breathy, vocal 'aah' pad, like a distant synthetic choir: the voice-like pads of 80s and 90s records.\n\nHow it's built: a saw and a pulse go through the State-Variable filter's band-pass with some RESONANCE: a single band, like a vowel formant, around 800 Hz. A little noise adds breath. Slow attack, a touch of Drive to bring the level up, Chorus (Ensemble), a large Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: slow chords in the middle of the keyboard.\n\nTweak: the filter's CUTOFF (move it to change the vowel: 400 'ooh', 800 'aah', 1500 'eeh'), RESONANCE, the breath level (mixer 3).",
